Subject: [PATCH 16/22] [M156] [FedCM] Return early in UpdateTaskId() if the
 view destroys it

Original change's description:
> [FedCM] Return early in UpdateTaskId() if the view destroys it
>
> IdentityDialogController::UpdateTaskId() lets the account selection view
> show its UI again when an actor task stops acting. The view can dismiss
> the UI synchronously, which can complete the request and destroy the
> controller, which then kept using its members. Return early if that
> happens.
>
> Fixed: 573931934
> Change-Id: Ie6bf46fd100629ae0ac53bd6139f5357cf50e1b5
> Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8757111
> Reviewed-by: Yi Gu <yigu@chromium.org>
> Commit-Queue: Ryan Qin <ryqin@chromium.org>
